The Linux Foundation Summit was moved now, going from Wednesday to 
Friday, June 13-15, to give more time to travel back during the weekend 
and to be back at work Monday morning.

It seems also that they do not do two-day workgroup meetings but only 
one-day meetings. see

http://www.linux-foundation.org/en/Linux_Foundation_Collaboration_Summit

and we are scheduled on the third day (now Friday). We will try to make 
call-in possible over the whole day.

So please everyone post here whether you want to come to Mountain View 
or not, so that I can make an estimatiuon of the room size.

I also would like to get some suggestions for what should be done on 
this day.

